**PASS.** I loaded the page cold at localhost:8000 in the Playwright browser and it starts cleanly. I found no loading or startup fault to send to a coder.

- **Build being tested:** The source and `dist/` hashes match the previous site review, and no rebuild was needed. The server on port 8000 (PID 13430) is this project's `dist/` server. It was already running before this review, so I left it running. All 7 files it serves match `dist/` exactly.
- **Loading:** All 7 files returned HTTP 200, with no failed requests, no page errors and no console errors. All 23 warnings are the browser refusing to start audio before a click or keypress, which is expected.
- **First image:** The title screen (TITLEPIC) appeared within 340 ms of starting navigation, with correct colours (checked from screenshots).
- **Speed:** During the demo the game advances at 34.89 tics per second (Doom's target is 35), with no stalls.
- **Menu and layout:** Escape opens and closes the main menu. The canvas keeps its 16:10 shape at 1280x720 and 800x600, with no scrollbars.
- **New this run:** The game's tic counter stops for about 1.2 s at roughly 5 s after load, when the title screen hands off to the demo. This is the engine's "melt" screen transition, not a hang:
  - the screen drew 40 different frames during the pause;
  - the browser's frame loop never paused more than 12 ms;
  - the engine's transition code (`d_main.c:308–326`) doesn't advance the tic counter while it runs.

  Any stall check covering the first ~6 s would wrongly flag this, so I've noted it for the tester.
- **Still open:**
  - The page title briefly reads "Doom (WASM)" before switching to "DOOM Shareware" (cosmetic, carried over for the coder).
  - Not checked: a clean rebuild, Firefox, Safari, high-DPI screens, a hidden tab and listening to audio.

The pass criteria are ones earlier agents proposed and you haven't approved them. Everything is in `artifacts/logs/reviewer_site.qchn1m/`; open `report.md` first.